This project fine-tunes and redistributes measurements of a derivative of Qwen.

Built with Qwen.

Qwen is licensed under the Qwen RESEARCH LICENSE AGREEMENT, Copyright (c) Alibaba Cloud.
All Rights Reserved. The base model is Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct; this project modifies
it by QLoRA fine-tuning on the BIRD training split (see prepared/manifest.json for the exact
examples). Research and non-commercial use only. Any distribution of the resulting weights
must carry the Qwen Research License text, this notice, and a statement of modification.

Training data come from the BIRD benchmark (https://bird-bench.github.io/), licensed
CC BY-SA 4.0: its training databases and the filtered split birdsql/bird23-train-filtered
(revision 4068469807b255fcfc0816bdd520946fe460d256).

Evaluation data are Arcwise-Plat-SQL (https://github.com/uiuc-kang-lab/text_to_sql_benchmarks)
by Tengjun Jin, Yoojin Choi, Yuxuan Zhu and Daniel Kang, "Pervasive Annotation Errors Break
Text-to-SQL Benchmarks and Leaderboards" (arXiv:2601.08778, VLDB 2026): BIRD Mini-Dev with a
corrected SQL answer key, building on Arcwise's corrections, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. It is read
from the measurement harness's data directory and is not redistributed here; the result files
in results/ contain question ids and the model's answers, not the dataset.

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository only; it does not cover the
model weights, which remain governed by the Qwen Research License.
